{#- Relief map window around a site (planning#18, docs/components.md). Set `map` (= record.map) and
    `mapHeadingId`. A fixed scale (Web Mercator, zoom 7) for every site: the tiles are plain images in a
    layer that CSS centres on the site, so the window works without JavaScript at any width. -#}
<figure class="site-map mb-0" aria-labelledby="{{ mapHeadingId }}-cap">
  <div class="site-map__frame site-map__frame--window" role="img"
    aria-label="Relief map of the area around {{ map.label }}, about 600 by 450 km, with rivers and natural lakes; north is up.">
    <div class="site-map__layer" style="left: calc(50% - {{ map.centerX | round(1) }}px); top: calc(50% - {{ map.centerY | round(1) }}px)">
      {%- for t in map.tiles %}
      <img src="{{ t.src }}" width="{{ map.tileSize }}" height="{{ map.tileSize }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="left: {{ t.x }}px; top: {{ t.y }}px" eleventy:ignore>
      {%- endfor %}
      {%- for x in map.sites %}
      <a class="site-map__marker{% if x.current %} site-map__marker--current{% endif %}" href="{{ x.path }}" style="left: {{ x.x | round(1) }}px; top: {{ x.y | round(1) }}px"{% if x.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
        <span class="site-map__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="site-map__label">{{ x.label }}</span>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="site-map__scale" style="width: {{ map.scale.px }}px" aria-hidden="true"><span>{{ map.scale.km }} km</span></div>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="{{ mapHeadingId }}-cap" class="small text-body-secondary mt-2">
    The same scale on every site page; the scale bar holds at the site's latitude. North is up. Rivers, natural lakes and
    coastlines as today; modern reservoirs are left out. Relief: Copernicus DEM GLO-90; rivers: HydroRIVERS; lakes and sea:
    Natural Earth (<a href="/data/#map-sources">sources</a>).
  </figcaption>
</figure>
